meta {
  name: Create Time Block
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/time-blocks
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Deep work",
    "startDateTime": "2026-09-24T13:00:00Z",
    "endDateTime": "2026-09-24T14:00:00Z"
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Time Block

  Creates a time block owned by the authenticated user. Returns 201.

  Requires ACCESS_TOKEN cookie (login/register first) + X-CSRF-Token header
  (the `csrfToken` env var is auto-filled by the login/register/refresh
  post-response script — never paste it manually).

  Optional fields: `projectId` (must belong to the user, else 404),
  `seriesId` (nullable UUID; not validated until SERIES-001). Not patchable.

  Returns 400 when title is blank/>200 chars or end <= start.

  NOTE: the backend log line "Request without Origin and Referer headers"
  is a harmless WARN (fail-open for non-browser clients like Bruno) — it does
  NOT block the request. Real failures come with HTTP status: 401 = login
  first, 403 = missing/wrong X-CSRF-Token.
}
